.Dd May 4, 2026
.Dt DIR_HASH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dir_hash::hash_directory
.Nd content-based directory tree hash with BLAKE3
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libdir_hash
(header-only; requires
.Lb libblake3
at link time)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dir_hash.hpp
.Bd -literal
namespace dir_hash {
inline namespace v1 {

template <typename Fn, typename ErrFn = detail::NoopError>
std::array<uint8_t, 32> hash_directory(
    std::string_view           path,
    Fn&&                       callback,
    ErrFn&&                    on_error = {},
    std::pmr::memory_resource* mem      =
        std::pmr::get_default_resource());

}}
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn hash_directory
walks the tree rooted at
.Fa path
with
.Xr fts 3 ,
hashes every regular file with BLAKE3, and computes a Merkle-style hash
for every directory by feeding the lexicographically-sorted multiset of
child hashes into BLAKE3.
The directory hash is name-agnostic: two directories whose files have
identical content \(em regardless of filenames or arrangement \(em hash
to the same value.
Symlinks and other non-regular entries are excluded.
An empty directory hashes to BLAKE3 of an empty input.
.Pp
.Fa callback
is invoked once per node as its hash is finalised, with signature
.Bd -literal -offset indent
void(std::string_view path,
     const std::array<uint8_t, 32>& hash,
     bool is_dir);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Fa path
passed to the callback is valid only for the duration of the call;
copy it if it must outlive the callback.
.Pp
.Fa on_error
is invoked for files or directories that cannot be read, with signature
.Bd -literal -offset indent
void(std::string_view path, std::error_code ec);
.Ed
.Pp
The offending node is skipped and does not contribute to its parent's
hash.
The default is a no-op.
.Pp
.Fa mem
governs all internal allocations \(em path buffer, child-hash
accumulators, and the 4 MiB read buffer.
It does not affect caller-side allocations.
.Sh I/O BEHAVIOUR
Every file is opened with
.Dv POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL
and closed with
.Dv POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED ,
which protects the ZFS ARC working set on
.Fx
and avoids polluting the page cache on Linux.
Files are read in 4 MiB chunks and fed to the BLAKE3 hasher
incrementally.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The 32-byte hash of the directory at
.Fa path .
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn hash_directory
throws
.Vt std::system_error
if
.Fa path
cannot be opened or is not a directory.
The contained
.Vt std::error_code
wraps the underlying
.Va errno
under
.Vt std::system_category .
.Pp
Per-file errors during traversal are reported via
.Fa on_error ;
the traversal continues.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Root hash only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
auto root = dir_hash::hash_directory(
    "/backup/2024-01",
    [](std::string_view, const std::array<uint8_t, 32>&, bool) {});
.Ed
.Pp
With a monotonic arena:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
std::pmr::monotonic_buffer_resource arena(64 * 1024);
auto root = dir_hash::hash_directory(
    "/backup/2024-01",
    [](std::string_view, const std::array<uint8_t, 32>&, bool) {},
    {},
    &arena);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dirhash 1 ,
.Xr fts 3 ,
.Xr posix_fadvise 2
.Sh STANDARDS
The library targets C++17.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Keith Williams .
